cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rgmin, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "rgmin: local minimization over eindir differentiable objectives"
authors:
  - family-names: Goswami
    given-names: Rohit
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2393-8056"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmniPotentRPC/rgmin"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: 2026-10-10
license: MIT
keywords:
  - optimization
  - conjugate-gradient
  - L-BFGS
  - trust-region
  - line-search
  - Rust
abstract: >-
  Local first-order and matrix-free second-order minimization in Rust
  over eindir differentiable objectives, with a DLPack-carrying C ABI.
  Line searches, quasi-Newton methods, trust regions with
  Steihaug-Toint CG, and a randomized Nystrom preconditioner, each
  pinned by Lean proofs of its exact algebra and by tests holding the
  implementation to them.
